<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyen Kim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1468–1545</span> · Also known as Nguyễn Kim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nguyen Kim was a Vietnamese general who led the loyalists of the Later Le dynasty against the Mac dynasty, which had usurped the throne in 1527. He restored a Le emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanh-hoa">Thanh Hoa</a> in 1533. After his death in 1545 his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinh-kiem">Trinh Kiem</a> took command, while his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-hoang">Nguyen Hoang</a> founded the line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyen lords</a> in the south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nguyen-kim.jpg" alt="Nguyen Kim" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kiennguyen546193 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tri%E1%BB%87u_T%E1%BB%95_Mi%E1%BA%BFu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
